      "problem": "What is the $5$th term of the geometric sequence given below?\n\n$$\nf(n+1)=-\\frac{1}{2}f(n),\\,f(1)=80,\\,n\\ge 1\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "We use the recursive formula to compute the terms of the sequence up to the $5$th term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1) & =80 \\\\ f(2) & =-\\frac{1}{2}f(1)=-\\frac{1}{2}(80)=-40 \\\\ f(3) & =-\\frac{1}{2}f(2)=-\\frac{1}{2}(-40)=20 \\\\ f(4) & =-\\frac{1}{2}f(3)=-\\frac{1}{2}(20)=-10 \\\\ f(5) & =-\\frac{1}{2}f(4)=-\\frac{1}{2}(-10)=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(5)=5.$",
